<article class="env-remark" id="87B4F1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/87B4F1">Remark <span data-tag="87B4F1">3.2.5.4</span>.</a> The simplicial set $\Nerve _{f}(\calC )$ of Definition <a href="/tag/DEB613" data-tag="DEB613">3.2.5.2</a> depends functorially on $f$. When $f$ takes the constant value $\Delta ^0$, there is a canonical isomorphism $\Nerve _{f}(\calC ) \simeq \Nerve (\calC )$. In particular, for <em>any</em> functor $f$, there is a canonical map $\Nerve _{f}(\calC ) \rightarrow \Nerve (\calC )$; the fiber of this map over an object $C \in \calC $ can be identified with the simpicial set $f(C)$. </p>
